tour graph-draw
kind flow
author ai
group gui/graph
note One frame of the graph canvas, in two halves. First App::graph_phase, run from App::frame before any view is built, while it still has the renderer's Measure: input against last frame's hit rectangles, the rebuild and layout, the camera, and a Scene built in window pixels. Every change it makes to GraphState is a GraphAction sent through App::apply, and the actions meant for the rest of the GUI (select a step, focus, go to a line, ask for a hover) come back in GraphFrame to be pushed by the view. Then the graph_tab view draws the toolbar and hands the Scene to one custom element, frame.canvas, whose closure paints it onto ui's Canvas when the tree is drawn. So there is no element per node and no hit testing from the element tree: the scene records its own hit rectangles and the next frame's clicks are resolved against them. Pan and zoom are two GraphState fields rather than a transform - the node font size is the UI size times the zoom, rounded to a whole pixel, so text is rasterised at the size it is drawn and never scaled. Sibling boxes are painted first, then edges, then nodes, so nodes sit on top: muted green curves for the steps of a tour, grey ones for the other calls, and an orange one for a callee drawn behind its caller along the graph's direction, looping back between the two nodes' facing sides. Every edge is routed for the direction: left to right it leaves and enters sideways, top to bottom through the bottom and top edges.

