file crates/gui/src/graph/scene.rs
symbol edges
lines 0 72
hash 8df0f1f07b62dd57
note The edges, routed by a Router for the graph's direction. Left to right a call edge leaves level with the line that makes the call when that line is shown, and from the header otherwise; top to bottom it leaves the middle of the node's bottom edge. An edge to a node ahead along the direction is a curve bowing forward into the target's entry (the header's left end, or the top middle), in EXPANSION_EDGE; a callee drawn behind its caller gets a BACK_EDGE curve bowing backwards between the facing sides instead of a wire across the canvas. Tour edges, parent step to child step, are drawn last, thicker and in STEP_EDGE, and carry no label - the node's number is the label. A self-call and a callee that is already the caller's child step get no call edge.

